00:37.160 --> 00:40.920
We still have some time 
until the bullet train arrives.

00:41.430 --> 00:44.920
Shall we buy something to drink, then?

00:44.920 --> 00:47.490
Certainly. We can buy boxed lunches, as well.

00:47.490 --> 00:48.440
All right.

00:48.940 --> 00:52.440
<b><i>Crab Three-Flavors Lunch</i></b>

00:48.940 --> 00:52.440
<b>Chicken Rice Lunch</b>

00:49.330 --> 00:51.650
They all look so good, it's hard to decide.

00:52.440 --> 00:54.270
"Lord of the Beef"?

00:54.270 --> 00:55.960
"Crab Three-Flavors Lunch"?

00:55.960 --> 00:57.890
"Chicken Rice Lunch"?

00:59.710 --> 01:01.180
I'm getting this.

00:59.950 --> 01:02.700
<b>Coastal Octopus Pot Lunch</b>

01:03.350 --> 01:05.200
"Coastal Octopus Pot Lunch"?

01:05.200 --> 01:07.980
I saw it in a magazine, 
and I've been curious about it.

01:10.010 --> 01:12.710
And the container makes a nice souvenir.

01:13.040 --> 01:15.450
You can even send away for a lid for it.

01:16.580 --> 01:18.970
Then I'll get this one, too.

01:18.970 --> 01:21.470
We'll have a matching set, then.

01:22.720 --> 01:23.970
Yes!

01:23.970 --> 01:24.980
<b>George the Kitten</b>

01:26.820 --> 01:29.480
<i>It's our third matching set!</i>

01:29.480 --> 01:31.490
<i>I love you, octopus pot!</i>

01:31.490 --> 01:34.520
<i>I'm startin' off this trip 
on one heckuva lucky foot!</i>

01:35.480 --> 01:36.500
<i>Oh, crud...</i>

01:36.500 --> 01:39.560
<i>Almost forgot I was doin' this for work.</i>

01:42.730 --> 01:45.170
<i>Pickin' boxed lunches is so much fun!</i>

